      "extract": "[]{#se:AtitDs label=\"se:AtitDs\"} Previously it was seen that in the high temperature deconfining phase of $SU(2)$ Yang-Mills theory there is a transition in the staggered Dirac spectrum from localized low modes to delocalized modes higher up in the spectrum [@Kovacs:2010wx]. The question we ask here is whether such a transition also occurs in real QCD with light dynamical quarks. This is a non-trivial question since",
