      "extract": "We have seen that the lowest eigenmodes spread out only to a distance scale below the inverse temperature. Therefore these modes cannot contribute to quark propagation on length scales larger than that. As far as hadronic correlators are considered above that distance scale the system behaves as if it had a gap of order $\\lambda_c$. The influence of this effective gap on the physics depends on how $\\lambda_c$, the",
